WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so happy you're here.
-I am so happy.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna say
straight off the bat,

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were fantastic
on the Golden Globes.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:07.073
-That's very kind of you to say.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were.
I was there as you know,

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:10.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I didn't get a chance
to give you a big hug

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:13.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
and say you were fantastic
whilst you were up and at 'em.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.347 line:92%
-Well, thank you so much.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.149
We actually met in this building
in 2005

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:17.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you hosted
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:20.420
Is it true that there's a sketch
you and I did together

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you still hear about
from people?

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.223 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I hear about it,

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I actually go on YouTube
or on the website.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:27.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You watch it yourself
a few times.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.094 line:92%
-Because it makes me chuckle

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:31.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I remember you
that time.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
That whole week was
one of the best,

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
most terrifying experiences
of my life.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:38.471
But you were so instrumental
in that of making me feel calm.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that sketch was one of
the funniest things

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.541 line:92%
I've ever, ever, ever done.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.943
-You brought me to a party with
your friends. We were on a date.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were on a date.
-That was a comedy joke.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.914 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was -- the party was
Bob Fosse-themed,

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:53.820
and I was the only person who
was not a Bob Fosse character.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.354 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:57.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, it was really --
-It went from --

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.826 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oopsie. Jazz.
-Yeah, jazz.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:03.997 line:92%
This is basically the character.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
My only recurring character
on "SNL"

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.268 size:88% position:44%
was a guy who was like,
"This isn't going well!"

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.903 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:12.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've done theater.
Do you miss the theater?

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.307 line:92%
Do you go see a lot of theater?

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:14.874 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, to all.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.143
I started in theater when I was
a little, little girl.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.446 size:88% position:44%
I was nine in "Annie,"
and I did "Bugsy Malone"

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:22.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
in like the Broadway,
in the West End in London.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.752
And then I did a lot of theater
in Britain,

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.853 line:92%
and then became TV and film.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:30.890
And then I went back about six,
seven years ago to Broadway,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I loved it.
I love, love, loved it.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.594 line:92%
And I always go to the theater.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.897
I sit there, and I sit, and as
the play, or the musical starts,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's like,
"I want to be up there.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:40.767 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I want to be up there."

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm just looking
for something --

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would love to do
something original.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
Something that has never been
done before, you know,

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.174 size:84% position:42% line:92%
so that would be great.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.442 line:92%
So I'm looking forward to that.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also --
You found this story,

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.679 line:92%
this Griselda Blanco story.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.013 line:92%
You were drawn to that as well.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
You kind of became
obsessed with her.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I became obsessed with her,
yeah.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.620
It's been three years of this
obsession with this woman.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How did you come
to know about her?

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.190 line:92%
-I saw a documentary called --

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:08.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was a well done
and well-viewed documentary

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.429 line:92%
called "Cocaine Cowboys."

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this woman
wasn't featured in it

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.633 line:92%
because she had since passed.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:17.070
But all these men,
these dark, very dangerous men,

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.004 line:92%
some of them out of prison,

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:21.941
some of them still in prison
and never coming out of prison,

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
talked about this woman,
Griselda Blanco.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they revered her.
They feared her.

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:30.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was like, "Who was this
woman who was running --"

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:33.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was
the queen of these kingpins.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:37.223 line:92%
Pablo Escobar worked for her.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.024 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, you know.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:38.958 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And she first of all,

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:42.328 size:84% position:42%
she survived so long
at the top in this game

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.263 size:78% position:39% line:92%
in the '70s in Miami,

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:46.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
where it was the height of
the drug industry.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:49.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was -- She was running
the show.

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You said she survived
for a long time.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it true that one of
the reasons,

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, there's very little tape
on her.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.543 line:92%
-I didn't see any tape of her

00:02:56.543 --> 00:03:01.047
except some old footage after
she'd been deported to Colombia.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was in her older years
not long

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
before she was
actually assassinated.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was
in a small apartment.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:10.023
She was very grandma-ish,
and she was, you know --

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.759
-That's how they get you.
That's how they get you.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:15.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I said I don't believe that
for one minute

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:16.863 line:92%
because this woman is an actor.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:19.799
She had everything that we just
strive for, you know.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:23.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was really screwed up
in many ways, but brilliant.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she came from Medellin
in Colombia.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:31.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
She became the head of
the drug industry in America.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:36.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she just had so many
different layers

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.317 line:92%
for me to play with, you know?

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.351 line:92%
-Audiences tend to be drawn to

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
these stories about
the drug trade.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:42.555
You were, I would argue, in one
of the greatest movies about it

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
of all-time -- "Traffic."
-Thank you.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And why do you think it is
that audiences

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
are drawn to stories
like Griselda's?

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:50.029
-Myself being one of those
audiences, what is it that we --

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.966
I mean, I'm always, and I'm sure
this -- I mean what are we,

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:53.533 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Godfather 4?"

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.336
There's a fascination with
the under -- a darker world.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:59.372
You know, a world that I'm never
going to be a part of,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there's something --
-You don't know!

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.577 line:92%
-Don't sell yourself short!

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:08.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Third time a charm as we say
in Ireland, you know?

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:10.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe the third one
will be real. No.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:14.387
It's just that world, the
family -- the family, you know.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.555 line:92%
-And Griselda was like that.

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:19.692
She hid behind the fact that she
could justify what she did.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:24.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was pretty gruesome
at times for the family

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.265 line:92%
just so her boys wouldn't --

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:28.201 size:84% position:42%
you know, live the life
that she had to live.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.736 line:92%
I don't buy that either, Seth.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really feel that
this woman was --

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, she was a very
powerful, but on a power trip.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:38.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, she -- she --
she had it all.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:39.646 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And she was an addict.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
So she had that addictive
personality,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.282 line:92%
and when she couldn't stop,

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:44.384
there was never enough money.
There was never enough greed.

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:47.053
There was never enough coke.
There was never enough sex.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was never enough
of anything.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.789
-You're telling my story.
You're telling my story.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:54.394
-I know. I'm renaming it
the return of Seth Meyers.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.362
-Well, you can play me hopefully
one day, too.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:57.830 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I will play you.

